{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["The sense of <b>but the children of Israel went up armed (וחמשים)</b> is to say that even though HaShem led them by way of the wilderness, they were afraid lest the Philistines, inhabitants of the cities near them, come upon them, so they went girded like those going forth to battle. And some say (Ibn Ezra) that Scripture informs that they went out with a high hand and expected to be redeemed, and they did not walk in the manner of slaves fleeing."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:50.721770758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}